{
  "rationale": "No race data exists yet (iteration 0), so this is a conservative baseline built from the contract's physics. Geometry: five sensors at 20 mm lateral spacing (x = -0.04 to +0.04) and 0.05 m ahead of the axle, so the line is seen by several sensors and the signal stays smooth. A 12 mm footprint is wider than the 20 mm gaps, which keeps readings overlapping and avoids dropouts on tight bends. Wheel track 0.12 m and radius 0.03 m give a moderate turn authority, body width 0.12 m leaves a comfortable off-track margin (limit about 0.09 m), and mass 0.8 kg keeps inertia low. Controller: weights -2,-1,0,1,2 map the lateral offset to a signal of about 1 per 2 cm. kp = 2 gives roughly 700 PWM of wheel differential per unit of signal, which is enough to correct without saturating. kd = 0.1 damps the oscillation that a pure P loop would cause at speed. ki = 0 avoids integral windup on the curves. base_speed = 1.6 is set to meet the roughly 1.5 m/s average needed to finish in under 3 s, with some margin for the slower bends. line_loss = last_direction lets the robot recover in the direction it was last turning when the tape is lost. Expected result: completion on the oval and s-bend, with the slalom the most likely source of line-loss events and rms error. Hypotheses to test: (1) base_speed 1.6 is fast enough to finish within 3 s without leaving the track; (2) kd = 0.1 is enough damping, and steering_oscillation stays low; (3) the rms error is dominated by the sharp slalom bends, so a higher kp or a wider sensor spread may be needed there.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.04, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": -0.02, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.02, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.04, "y": 0.05}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.012,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.12,
    "body_length": 0.16,
    "mass": 0.8
  },
  "controller": {
    "base_speed": 1.6,
    "kp": 2.0,
    "ki": 0.0,
    "kd": 0.1,
    "sensor_weights": [-2, -1, 0, 1, 2],
    "line_loss": "last_direction"
  },
  "observation_request": {
    "measurements": [
      "completion",
      "progress",
      "completion_time",
      "rms_error",
      "max_error",
      "line_loss_events",
      "steering_oscillation"
    ]
  },
  "_presentation": {
    "entity0": {
      "label": "Baseline 5-sensor P+D bot",
      "notes": "First candidate, built from contract physics with no race data yet: five 12 mm sensors at 20 mm spacing, kp 2, kd 0.1, base_speed 1.6 to meet the sub-3 s finish. Expected to complete the oval and s-bend, with slalom the likely weak point for rms error and line loss."
    }
  }
}
